{
  // The arena maps: where duels (/arena) are fought. Every duel gets an instance of its own of one of the enabled maps,
  // picked at random, so any number of duels can use the same map at once. See docs/arena.md.
  // This is read once, when the server starts. A mistake in one map is logged ([ARENA] ...) and only leaves that map out.
  // An admin can look around a map without a duel with /instance open arena:<name>.
  //
  // A map is:
  //   "name":        letters, digits, - and _. Its instance template is called arena:<name>.
  //   "description": what players are told it is called.
  //   "enabled":     false keeps it out of duels (it is still set up, so it can be looked at). Default true.
  //   "landblocks":  the landblocks of the map, written as the first four digits of a cell: 0x00670117 is landblock 0067.
  //   "bufferRing":  0 to 2 landblocks around them that are loaded as a margin players are turned back from. 0 for a dungeon,
  //                  at least 1 outdoors (where there are no walls). Default 0.
  //   "starts":      at least two places fighters are put at. Every fighter in a duel gets a different one, at random.
  //                  A cell, x, y, z, and the rotation as qx, qy, qz, qw (qw 1 and the others 0 is no rotation). /myloc shows them.
  //   "center", "radius": outdoors, the fighting area. A fighter who stays more than radius meters from the center
  //                  for 5 seconds is disqualified. Every start has to be inside it. Not needed for a dungeon.
  //
  // An outdoor map, for the curated list (remove the // to use it, and put in real coordinates):
  //
  // {
  //   "name": "example-field",
  //   "description": "a field",
  //   "landblocks": [ "A9B4" ],
  //   "bufferRing": 1,
  //   "center": { "cell": "0xA9B40021", "x": 96, "y": 96, "z": 20, "qw": 1 },
  //   "radius": 40,
  //   "starts": [
  //     { "cell": "0xA9B40021", "x": 76, "y": 96, "z": 20, "qw": 1 },
  //     { "cell": "0xA9B40021", "x": 116, "y": 96, "z": 20, "qw": 1 }
  //   ]
  // },

